    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d61">

                <pb facs="0158" n="58" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg58"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6315/3</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-02-01">February 1, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Austrian Minister<anchor n="39" xml:id="d61-f1"/> called to inform me
                    officially of the arrival on February 15th of an Austrian Trade Commission,
                    which will consist of four members and a secretary. The Minister mentioned the
                    name of three members—Mr. Boehler, president of the Boehler Foundry Company; Mr.
                    Kuffler, president of the largest textile undertaking, and Mr.
                        Granichstadten.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d61-f2"/> The secretary is Count
                    Seefried, a great-grandson of Emperor Francis Joseph. The mission will remain in
                    the United States for one month. From New York they will come to Washington,
                    then proceed to St. Louis, Chicago, etc., etc.</p>
                <pb facs="0159" n="59" xml:id="pg59"/>
                <p>The Minister has just received instructions to delay his scheduled leave of
                    absence for one month, that is, until the Trade Commission terminates its
                    work.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d61-f1" n="39" xml:id="d61-f1-content">
                <p>Edgar L. G. Prochnik.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d61-f2" n="40" xml:id="d61-f2-content">
                <p>The fourth member of the delegation was Mr. Hans Geggenhofer.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
